{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 31, "model_name": "nvidia/llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1", "content": "i am writing a detailed review of the movie \"the social network\" in all lower case letters as per your request.\n\n**movie title:** the social network\n**director:** david fincher\n**release year:** 2010\n\n**summary:**\nthe social network is a biographical drama film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent legal battles faced by its co-founder and first ceo, mark zuckerberg. the movie is based on the book \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben mezrich.\n\n**story:**\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a harvard university student, creating a website called \"facemash\" that compares the photos of two students and asks visitors to vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge success but also gets zuckerberg into trouble.\n\nlater, zuckerberg is approached by cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), who ask him to work on a social networking site for harvard students. zuckerberg agrees but eventually creates his own site, \"thefacebook\", with the help of eduard savarain (played by andrew garfield).\n\nas facebook gains popularity, zuckerberg faces legal challenges from the winklevoss twins, who claim that he stole their idea. simultaneously, the relationship between zuckerberg and savarain deteriorates due to disagreements over the direction of the company.\n\n**acting:**\n- jesse eisenberg delivers a brilliant performance as mark zuckerberg, capturing his intensity, arrogance, and vulnerability.\n- andrew garfield shines as eduard savarain, bringing depth to the character.\n- armie hammer successfully plays the dual role of the winklevoss twins.\n\n**direction and cinematography:**\ndavid fincher's direction is impeccable, with a perfect balance of drama and tension. the cinematography is sleek and modern, complementing the theme of the movie.\n\n**music:**\nthe soundtrack, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is haunting and perfectly complements the mood of the film.\n\n**critique:**\nwhile the movie is engaging and well-made, some characters feel somewhat one-dimensional. additionally, the portrayal of mark zuckerberg has been controversial, with some arguing that it is unfair.\n\n**rating:** 4.5/5\n\n**recommendation:**\nthe social network is a must-watch for anyone interested in the tech industry, social media, or compelling character studies. however, viewers should be aware that the film's accuracy has been disputed by some of the real-life individuals portrayed.\n\n**final thoughts:**\nthe social network is a well-crafted film that explores the complexities of success, friendship, and betrayal. despite its flaws, it is an engaging and thought-provoking watch.", "logprobs": [{"token": "i", "logprob": -0.04139022156596184}, {"token": " am", "logprob": -1.401969075202942}, {"token": " writing", "logprob": -0.04201051965355873}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.28195297718048096}, {"token": " detailed", "logprob": -0.07031776010990143}, {"token": " review", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -5.960462772236497e-07}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -5.4834770708112046e-05}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -1.9073468138230965e-06}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -4.0531076592742465e-06}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.011356238275766373}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.06699658930301666}, {"token": " all", "logprob": -0.0007390628452412784}, {"token": " lower", "logprob": -0.0021877181716263294}, {"token": " case", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": " letters", "logprob": -1.6005100011825562}, {"token": " as", "logprob": -8.046303264563903e-05}, {"token": " per", "logprob": -0.38689878582954407}, {"token": " your", "logprob"